WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.380
MongoDB security review should start with data flow, not only with a connection URI.

2
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:22.200
Identify every component that can read or write data: API routes, GraphQL resolvers, workers, scripts, admin tools, test utilities, import jobs, export jobs, dashboards, webhooks, and third-party integrations.

3
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.660
Then map the source of each value that reaches those operations.

4
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:40.320
Route parameters, query strings, request bodies, headers, cookies, uploaded files, queue messages, webhook payloads, configuration, and existing database records can all influence behavior.

5
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:45.880
Externally supplied values remain security-relevant even after they are stored.

6
00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:55.500
A value accepted from a customer today may be read from MongoDB tomorrow and used in an export, aggregation, notification, or admin workflow.

7
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:59.680
Treat it according to origin and purpose, not according to where it currently lives.

8
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:17.860
Sensitive collections and fields deserve specific attention: users, sessions, tokens, roles, tenant records, billing data, audit data, private documents, security settings, and operational metadata all carry different exposure and integrity risks.

9
00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:32.860
Trust boundaries exist between clients, Node.js services, MongoDB clusters, identity providers, secret stores, object storage, logging systems, CI/CD, administrators, and support users.

10
00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:37.840
Attach security requirements to collections, operations, and workflows.

11
00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:39.700
Who can cause this read.

12
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.480
Who can cause this update.

13
00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:43.580
What authorization is checked.

14
00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.360
What fields return to the caller.

15
00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:48.260
Which database identity runs the operation.

16
00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:54.680
These questions turn MongoDB security from vague concern into concrete reviewable behavior.
